{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"As of November 6, 2026:\n\n- **Fixed transaction fees** generally cover custody, transfer-agent, clearing/settlement and administrative costs of processing a creation/redemption order, often regardless of how many creation units it contains.\n- **Variable charges** generally offset transaction-specific costs—brokerage, bid–ask spreads, market impact, taxes or foreign exchange—particularly for cash transactions or cash substitutions, protecting existing shareholders from dilution.\n- **Who pays:** The authorized participant (AP) is ordinarily responsible to the fund or designated recipient. It may pass these costs to its client or incorporate them into its quoted price.\n- **Recipients may differ:** For example, the fixed fee may go to the custodian, while the variable charge goes to the fund. The prospectus and AP agreement govern.\n\n**Worth knowing:** These fund-imposed charges are distinct from an AP’s separately negotiated compensation, commissions or trading spread; they are not automatically AP revenue."}}
